        ],
        "summary": "codex exec auto-loads the host repo's AGENTS.md: in a repo that routes all agent work through the flow-next skills, the reviewer adopted that role and re-dispatched the review at itself, which the sandbox rejected (route A). With the flow-next codex plugin installed, the reviewer also read the plugin's own coordinator skills - 'never self-declares a verdict' - completed a good review, and withheld the tag (route B). The only counter-instruction flow-next ships, the persona preamble, was gated behind needs_persona_override=False for codex - a value that mechanically preserved pre-refactor behavior, never a decision. The plan prompt was also the only review prompt without the 'You ARE the reviewer' anchor (#246 gave it to the other three), which is why plan reviews failed first. And every no-verdict turn was misclassed as a transport timeout (the ladder scanned the reviewer's own output for the word 'timeout'), terminating in advice to repair a healthy backend.",
        "taskIds": [],
        "title": "Thirteen healthy runs, zero verdicts, and advice to repair the wrong thing"
